38	{"narrative":{"format_version":2,"base_sha":"56718fa809a3223b27fbe877855ca32b520eadad","head_sha":"9d9347361b47ede14bfbf8f58b0637b3a191b933","title":"Shared full-content rows reuse `RoamDiscourseNodeData` and carry their node type","situation":"When Roam sync uploads a shared node's full markdown, `getSharedRoamNodesWithFullContentUpdatesSince` finds the node type whose format matches the page title, and `fullContentNodeToCrossApp` turns the row into a `CrossAppNode`. On main the row was a `RoamFullContentNode`, a second flat row type that copied the node type's `format` onto every row.","before":"Each update was `{ fullContentNode: RoamFullContentNode, nodeTypeId }`. The row held `node_type_id` and a copy of `format`, and only the bare rows reached the converter.","after":"Each update is `{ fullContentNode: RoamDiscourseNodeData, nodeType: DiscourseNode }`. The row holds `type`, and the converter takes the matched `DiscourseNode` as a second argument and reads `format` from it. `RoamDiscourseNodeData` now types its times as `number` and drops the unread `author_name`.","boundary":"Type-only. The `CrossAppNode` the converter produces, the Content rows sync uploads and the write calls are unchanged. The full-content query still returns rows, not `CrossAppNode`; that and replacing `RoamDiscourseNodeData` are later ENG-2165 steps.","verification":"Code tracing showed the node type id and `format` still come from one regex match in the producer, so the converter's inputs are the same values as before. `tsc`, the three changed test files (46 tests) and the full Roam suite (710 tests) pass at the head. The `coreTitle` tests use the converter fixture below. No live Roam sync was run, and the author's Loom (shared with the ENG-1824 stack) wasn't watched.","demos":["https://www.loom.com/share/aa92dec129b644a1b3b308dfe32cb480"],"steps":[{"id":"s1","title":"Row type","text":"`RoamDiscourseNodeData` types `created` and `last_modified` as `number` and loses `author_name`.","s