th":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","hunk":"f-e174147fd1757fea-h3","layer":"layer-converter","line":86,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/9d9347361b47ede14bfbf8f58b0637b3a191b933/apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts#L86"},{"id":"s6","title":"Tests pass the format through the node type","text":"The regex-metacharacter case overrides `format` on the node type instead of on the row.","symbol":"fullContentNodeToCrossApp coreTitle","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/roamToCrossAppConverters.test.ts","hunk":"f-91cb11dcf767bdaf-h1","layer":"layer-converter","line":171,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/9d9347361b47ede14bfbf8f58b0637b3a191b933/apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/roamToCrossAppConverters.test.ts#L171"}],"example":{"title":"One Claim row, before and after","step_id":"s5","description":"The same row and node type from the converter test fixture, as each version passes them to `fullContentNodeToCrossApp`.","panels":[{"label":"Before: one argument (RoamFullContentNode)","code":"fullContentNodeToCrossApp({\n  source_local_id: \"node-1\",\n  created: 1000,\n  last_modified: 2000,\n  text: \"CLM - claim\",\n  node_type_id: \"schema-1\",\n  format: \"CLM - {content}\"\n})"},{"label":"After: row plus node type","code":"fullContentNodeToCrossApp(\n  {\n    source_local_id: \"node-1\",\n    created: 1000,\n    last_modified: 2000,\n    text: \"CLM - claim\",\n    type: \"schema-1\"\n  },\n  { type: \"schema-1\", text: \"Claim\", format: \"CLM - {content}\", ... }\n)"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Both versions","text":"`nodeType: \"schema-1\"`, `coreTitle: \"claim\"`, `content.direct.value: \"CLM - claim\"`."},{"label":"What moved","text":"`format` lives on the node type instead of on every row."}],"note":"Values from `roamToCrossAppConverters.test.ts` (`baseNode` and `claimSchema`); `author_local_id` omitted on both sides. Illustrative, not an observed production row."},"pseudocode":{"title":"Where `nodeType` and `format` come from","step_id":"s2","before":"for row in sharedRowsSince:\n  match = first node type whose format regex matches row.text\n  update = { fullContentNode: { ...row, node_type_id: match.type, format: match.format },\n             nodeTypeId: match.type }\nconvert(updates.map(u => u.fullContentNode)):\n  nodeType  = node.node_type_id\n  coreTitle = extractContentFromTitle(node.format, title)","after":"for row in sharedRowsSince:\n  match = first node type whose format regex matches row.text\n  update = { fullContentNode: { ...row, type: match.type }, nodeType: match }\nconvert(updates):\n  for { fullContentNode, nodeType } in updates:\n    nodeType  = fullContentNode.type\n    coreTitle = extractContentFromTitle(nodeType.format, title)","unchanged":"`sharedNodeTypeIds`, `content.direct`, `content.full`, the times and the upload path produce the same values."}}}
39	{"pseudocode":{"base_sha":"56718fa809a3223b27fbe877855ca32b520eadad","head_sha":"9d9347361b47ede14bfbf8f58b0637b3a191b933","title":"From the matched node type to the `CrossAppNode`","intro":"Read the change in data-flow order: the row type, the producer that pairs each row with its node type, the sync code that passes the pairs on, and the converter that reads `format` from the node type. Tests come last.","flow":["`RoamDiscourseNodeData` row type","`SharedFullContentUpdate` holds the `DiscourseNode`","Producer pairs row and node type","Sync passes the pairs","`upsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets` takes the pairs","`convertRoamNodeToFullContent` unpacks each pair","`fullContentNodeToCrossApp(node, schema)`","Tests"],"boundary":"Type-only. The produced `CrossAppNode`, uploaded Content rows and write calls are unchanged. Returning `CrossAppNode` from the query and replacing `RoamDiscourseNodeData` stay for later ENG-2165 steps.","steps":[{"title":"Row type: numeric times, no `author_name`","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/getAllDiscourseNodesSince.ts","line":10,"side":"head","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/coreTitleBackfill.test.ts"],"narrative":"`RoamDiscourseNodeData` becomes the row type for full-content updates too. `created` and `last_modified` are typed `number` because Roam returns `:create/time` and `:edit/time` as epoch milliseconds; the old `string` type never matched runtime values. `author_name` goes because nothing reads it from these rows. The queries still select `author_name`, which is harmless. The backfill test fixture follows the new shape.","code":"type RoamDiscourseNodeData = {\n  author_local_id, source_local_id, text, type: string\n  created, last_modified: number      // was string\n  node_title?: string\n  // author_name removed\n}"},{"title":"`SharedFullContentUpdate` holds the `DiscourseNode`","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/convertRoamNodeToFullContent.ts","line":8,"side":"head","narrative":"The update type moves from `syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts` to `convertRoamNodeToFullContent.ts`, because the converter now takes it as input. It holds the matched `DiscourseNode` instead of only its id, and `RoamFullContentNode` is deleted.","code":"// before (syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts)\ntype SharedFullContentUpdate = { fullContentNode: RoamFullContentNode, nodeTypeId: string }\n\n// after (convertRoamNodeToFullContent.ts, exported)\ntype SharedFullContentUpdate = { fullContentNode: RoamDiscourseNodeData, nodeType: DiscourseNode }"},{"title":"Producer pairs row and node type","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":1183,"side":"head","narrative":"`getSharedRoamNodesWithFullContentUpdatesSince` still drops rows whose title matches no node type. For a match, it sets `type` on the row and the whole `DiscourseNode` on the update, both from the same `matchingNodeType`. The row no longer gets a `format` copy. `node_title` is never set here, before or after.","code":"match = typeMatchers.find(regex matches row.text)?.node\nif no match: skip row\nreturn {\n  fullContentNode: { author_local_id, source_local_id, created,\n                     last_modified: max(node_edit_time, page_edit_time),\n                     text, type: match.type },\n  nodeType: match\n}"},{"title":"Sync passes the pairs","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":1495,"side":"head","narrative":"`createOrUpdateDiscourseEmbedding` builds `sharedNodeTypeIds` from `update.nodeType.type`, the same id the old `nodeTypeId` held. The intermediate array of bare rows is gone; the updates go straight to the full-content upload.","code":"sharedNodeTypeIds = Set(updates.map(u => u.nodeType.type))   // was u.nodeTypeId\nupsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets({ nodes: updates, ... })   // was updates.map(u => u.fullContentNode)"},{"title":"`upsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets` takes the pairs","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":820,"side":"head","narrative":"Only the input type changes. The `upsertFullContent` and `publishSharedNodeAssets` phases, the upload and the asset publish behave as before.","code":"upsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets({ nodes: SharedFullContentUpdate[], ... })\n  converted = convertRoamNodeToFullContent({ nodes })   // timed as upsertFullContent\n  upload(converted.content)\n  publishNodeAssets(converted.node)                    // timed as publishSharedNodeAssets"},{"title":"`convertRoamNodeToFullContent` unpacks each pair","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/convertRoamNodeToFullContent.ts","line":26,"side":"head","narrative":"The loop destructures each update and passes both halves to the converter. A failure for one node is still logged with its `source_local_id` and skipped.","code":"for { fullContentNode, nodeType } in nodes:\n  try:\n    crossAppNode = fullContentNodeToCrossApp(fullContentNode, nodeType)\n    content = crossAppNodeToDbContent(crossAppNode, \"full\")\n    keep { node: crossAppNode, content } if content defined\n  catch: log fullContentNode.source_local_id, skip"},{"title":"`fullContentNodeToCrossApp(node, schema)`","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","line":86,"side":"head","narrative":"The converter gains a second parameter. `coreTitle` uses `schema.format`; `nodeType` uses `node.type`. Both values come from the producer's single match, so the output equals the old output. The node type id now exists in two places on the update (`fullContentNode.type` and `nodeType.type`); they agree because one producer sets both.","code":"fullContentNodeToCrossApp(node: RoamDiscourseNodeData, schema: DiscourseNode):\n  title = node.node_title ?? node.text\n  nodeType  = node.type                                   // was node.node_type_id\n  coreTitle = extractContentFromTitle(schema.format, title) // was node.format\n  content   = { direct: title, full: buildFullInlineContent(uid, title) }"},{"title":"Tests follow the new shapes","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/roamToCrossAppConverters.test.ts","line":137,"side":"head","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/syncSharedNodeAssets.test.ts"],"narrative":"The `coreTitle` tests pass `claimSchema` as the node type, and the regex-metacharacter case overrides `format` on the node type. The asset-sync test builds a `claimType` node type and passes `{ fullContentNode, nodeType }`. Its mock of the converter ignores the second argument, so that test checks the pipeline shape, not `coreTitle`.","code":"fullContentNodeToCrossApp(baseNode, claimSchema)              -> coreTitle \"claim\"\nfullContentNodeToCrossApp(row, { ...claimSchema, format: \"Claim (draft) - {content}\" })\nupsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets({ nodes: [{ fullContentNode: sharedNode, nodeType: claimType }] })"}]}}
