22	{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","summary":"No `upsert_content` call left in Roam, including test harnesses","text":"There is no `upsert_content` call left in the Roam codebase, including test harnesses.","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Done When","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met with the stack. At head, `git grep upsert_content -- apps/roam` finds nothing; the base had 7 matches. This PR removes the two sync writers in `syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts`, the duplicate in `upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts`, and the references in `fileReferenceHarness.ts` and `syncSharedNodeAssets.test.ts`. #1578 removed the node-type writer.","verification":"Grep check at the pinned head; Roam unit suite passes (715 tests).","layer_ids":["layer-embed","layer-write","layer-sync","layer-reembed"],"check_ids":["check-8","check-7"],"code_links":[{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":700,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts","line":41,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/fixtures/fileReferenceHarness.ts","line":82,"side":"head"}],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-2","summary":"Content computations go through `CrossAppNode`","text":"Unify the Content computations to create the CrossAppNode type","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Solution (first half)","source_kind":"paraphrased","assessment_status":"partial","assessment":"Partly met. Node instances now build every Content through `discourseNodeToCrossApp`/`fullContentNodeToCrossApp` and `crossAppNodeToDbConcept`, the converter publish uses. Node-type Content still comes from `convertRoamNodeToLocalContent` inside `discourseNodeSchemaToLocalConcept`'s row. #1578's approved body defers that to ENG-2165 because `CrossAppNodeSchema` has no Content, so this is a documented deferral, not a defect in this PR.","verification":"Code inspection of the converters and `convertDgToSupabaseConcepts`; converter unit tests pass.","layer_ids":["layer-convert","layer-write"],"check_ids":["check-6"],"code_links":[{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","line":74,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":700,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":652,"side":"head"}],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-3","summary":"Each node is sent in a single call","text":"send it, after conversion, in a single call.","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Solution (second half)","source_kind":"paraphrased","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met. Each node's Concept and its Contents travel in one `upsert_concepts` row (`contents_inline`); calls are batched 50 rows at a time. In `upsert_concepts` the Concept insert and its inline `upsert_content` share one exception block, so a failing Content rolls the Concept back and the row returns -2.","verification":"Payload tests in convertDgToSupabaseConcepts.test.ts; rollback behavior read from concept.sql at head, not executed against a database.","layer_ids":["layer-write"],"check_ids":["check-6","check-12"],"code_links":[{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":700,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":312,"side":"head"}],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-4","summary":"Write straight to `upsert_concepts`; leave publish alone","text":"Don't wait for FEE-890. Write each node in one `upsert_concepts` call, directly to the database. ... Moving Roam sync and publish onto the route comes later in its own tickets, so this ticket doesn't move publish.","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Comment: Decision (Sid, 2026-10-22); Marc-Antoine agreed 2026-10-23","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met. Sync calls `supabaseClient.rpc(\"upsert_concepts\")` directly; no route is added, and `publishNodesToGroups.ts` is not in the diff.","verification":"Diff inspection.","layer_ids":["layer-write"],"check_ids":[],"code_links":[{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":312,"side":"head"}],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-5","summary":"No data migration","text":"No data migration. The first sync after a graph loads already re-sends half-written nodes (ENG-1793).","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Comment: Decision (Sid, 2026-10-22)","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met. The diff has no migration or SQL change. Existing first-child nodes gain their `direct` Content only when sync next sends them (a change, the core-title backfill, or Generate & upload all node embeddings).","verification":"Diff inspection; no files under packages/database changed.","layer_ids":["layer-sync"],"check_ids":[],"code_links":[],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-6","summary":"The suggestive-rules re-embed stops being a Content-only write","text":"The suggestive-rules setting: `DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx:61` re-embeds block nodes through `upsertNodesToSupabaseAsContentWithEmbeddings` (`syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:760`), a Content-only write.","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Comment: Scope note (Sid, 2026-10-22)","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met. Update embeddings now calls `upsertNodesWithEmbeddings`, which writes the node type's schema Concept and each node's Concept with its Contents through `upsert_concepts`. It also drops unresolved Sources and shows a toast on failure.","verification":"Unit test 'embeds the description of a block-backed node and the title of a page node'; the author's proof kit reports the button cases passing on identical code.","layer_ids":["layer-reembed"],"check_ids":["check-6","check-10"],"code_links":[{"path":"apps/roam/src/components/settings/DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx","line":62,"side":"head"},{"path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":792,"side":"head"}],"finding_ids":[],"assessment_base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","assessment_head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3"},{"id":"req-7","summary":"A node no longer lands half-written","text":"Roam sync writes Concepts and Content in separate calls, to `upsert_concepts` and `upsert_content`. If one call fails, we have partially defined nodes in the database.","source_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-1824/use-the-unified-upsert-concepts-in-roam","source_section":"Problem","source_kind":"paraphrased","assessment_status":"met","assessment":"Met for node instances and node types. A row failure now leaves neither the Concept nor its Contents. `omitMissingSources` keeps an unresolved Source from failing a row that would otherwise land, and every batch is still sent. A node whose row keeps failing (for example a -1 name conflict) no longer gets its Content refreshed; that is the intended trade.","verification":"Batch and row-failure tests pass; database rollback semantics read from SQL, n