32	{"quick_summary":{"problem":"Roam sync writes a node's Concept and its Content in separate calls, `upsert_concepts` and `upsert_content`. When one call fails, the database holds a half-written node.","solution":"Convert each Roam node to a `CrossAppNode` and write it with `crossAppNodeToDbConcept`, the converter publish uses. The Concept carries its `direct`, description and full Contents in one `upsert_concepts` row. The Update embeddings button uses the same write.","source":"Authored paraphrase of ENG-1824 Problem/Solution and the pinned diff."}}
33	{"intent_source_text":"ENG-1824 Done When (verbatim):\n* There is no `upsert_content` call left in the Roam codebase, including test harnesses.\n\nSolution (verbatim):\n* Remove the calls to `upsert_content`. Unify the Content computations to create the CrossAppNode type, and send it, after conversion, in a single call.\n\nDecision (Sid, 2026-10-22, verbatim):\n- Don't wait for FEE-890. Write each node in one `upsert_concepts` call, directly to the database. This departs from the 2026-07-17 agreement, because the route has no date. Moving Roam sync and publish onto the route comes later in its own tickets, so this ticket doesn't move publish.\n- This ticket is a step of ENG-2165, which becomes the parent. It comes after ENG-2061 and converts through `CrossAppNode`, as its Solution says, so Roam sync and publish share one conversion.\n- No data migration. The first sync after a graph loads already re-sends half-written nodes (ENG-1793).\n\nScope note (Sid, 2026-10-22, verbatim):\n\"no `upsert_content` call left in the Roam codebase\" also covers two Content-only writes that the Notes don't list.\n- Node type Content: `upsertNodeSchemaToContent` (`apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:602`, called at `:682`) writes each node type's Content separately from its schema Concept.\n- The suggestive-rules setting: `DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx:61` re-embeds block nodes through `upsertNodesToSupabaseAsContentWithEmbeddings` (`syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:760`), a Content-only write.\n\nSplit across the stack (from the PR bodies): #1577 adds `content.directAndDescription` to `CrossAppNode`; #1578 moves node-type Content into the schema Concept; #1579 removes the remaining `upsert_content` calls."}
34	{"scope_review":{"base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3","status":"assessed","summary":"Six additions beyond Done When. Five are required to keep sync correct once Content rides inside the Concept. One needs a recorded decision: sync now writes a plain `direct` Content for unpublished first-child nodes, which ENG-2426 lists as Out of Scope.","entries":[{"title":"Plain `direct` Content for every first-child node, published or not","summary":"`crossAppNodeToDbConcept` always emits `direct` because the Concept name comes from it, and #1577 (approved) kept `direct` as the page title by adding `directAndDescription`. So first-child nodes now get a `direct` Content without an embedding. For published nodes this meets ENG-2426's Done When. For unpublished nodes it goes past ENG-2426's Out of Scope (Ticket Draft). The PR's Scope check says the decision isn't recorded in Linear. Leaving `direct` out for unpublished nodes would need a publish-status filter, so keeping it is defensible; it needs a Decision comment and an ENG-2426 update.","kind":"unclear","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-2","req-3"],"decision_url":"https://linear.app/discourse-graphs/issue/ENG-2426/roam-sync-leaves-a-published-nodes-direct-content-stale-when-its-type","code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts#L89","label":"roamToCrossAppConverters.ts:89"},{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts#L95","label":"roamToCrossAppConverters.ts:95"}]},{"title":"Drop a Source the space can't resolve before the upsert","summary":"With Content inside the Concept row, an unresolved `sourceDocument` would fail the whole row (-2) and take the Content with it. `omitMissingSources` keeps a RID, a Source in the same upsert, or an existing Concept, which is publish's `omitMissingSource` rule. The node is written without the reference until it is next sent with its Source available.","kind":"supporting","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-7"],"code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L772","label":"syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:772"}]},{"title":"Send every batch and gate assets on rows that landed","summary":"Main stopped at the first failed batch, but Content had already gone out through `upsert_content`. Now Content rides in the batches, so stopping early would hold back later nodes' Content. `ConceptRowFailuresError` carries the failed `source_local_id`s so `publishNodeAssets` skips them (FileReference has a foreign key to Content).","kind":"supporting","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-7"],"code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L323","label":"syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:323"},{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L844","label":"syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:844"}]},{"title":"Shared nodes sent only for full content now also upsert their Concept","summary":"The full Content can only travel inside a Concept row, so these nodes' Concepts are rewritten with `last_modified` = max(node edit, page edit), as publish computes it.","kind":"supporting","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-3"],"code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L744","label":"syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:744"}]},{"title":"Concept batch size 200 to 50","summary":"Each row now carries its Contents and embedding (about 33 KB per embedded node per the PR body), so 50 rows match the old per-call `upsert_content` payload. PR #1333 chose the same size.","kind":"supporting","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-3"],"code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L70","label":"syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts:70"}]},{"title":"Update embeddings writes Concepts and shows a failure toast","summary":"Routing the re-embed through `upsert_concepts` (scope note 2026-10-22) means it writes the node type's schema Concept and each node's Concept. The new `catch` sends failures to `internalError`, which the new row-failure error needs; before, a rejection went unhandled.","kind":"supporting","required_now":true,"requirement_ids":["req-6"],"code_links":[{"url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/components/settings/DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx#L72","label":"DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx:72"}]}]}}
