38	{"narrative":{"format_version":2,"base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3","title":"One upsert_concepts row per Roam node","situation":"Roam sync wrote a node's Content with `upsert_content` and its Concept with `upsert_concepts`, so either could land without the other. Publish already wrote both in one call through `crossAppNodeToDbConcept`.","before":"Sync built Content rows with `convertRoamNodeToLocalContent` and Concepts with `discourseNodeBlockToLocalConcept`, and sent them in separate RPCs. A first-child node got only a `direct_and_description` Content. Update embeddings wrote Content only.","after":"Sync and Update embeddings build a `CrossAppNode` per node and send its Concept with `contents_inline` in one `upsert_concepts` row, 50 rows per call. A first-child node gets `direct` (page title) and `direct_and_description` (with the embedding). Failed rows are collected, and assets run only for rows that landed.","boundary":"Covers Roam sync and the Update embeddings button only. Publish, Obsidian (ENG-1823), the FEE-890 route and PATCH semantics (ENG-2166) are unchanged, and node-type Content still uses `discourseNodeSchemaToLocalConcept`. There is no migration: a stored first-child node gains its `direct` Content when sync next sends it.","demos":["https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70f71dc1-9cb2-4e25-a7da-31f705822369","https://www.loom.com/share/aa92dec129b644a1b3b308dfe32cb480","https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/pull/1579#issuecomment-6414810194"],"steps":[{"id":"s1","title":"Map a Roam row to a CrossAppNode","text":"`discourseNodeToCrossApp` sets `direct` to the page title and, when the row has `node_title`, adds `directAndDescription` (title plus first child, credited to the child's creator). The Source slot comes from the page title.","symbol":"discourseNodeToCrossApp","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","hunk":"f-e174147fd1757fea-h1","layer":"layer-convert","line":74,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts#L74"},{"id":"s2","title":"Credit the page creator","text":"The first-child query gains `node_author_local_id` (the page's `:create/user`, falling back to the child's), so the Concept author stays the page creator as `getNodeExtraData` gave on main.","symbol":"getDiscourseNodeTypeWithSettingsBlockNodes","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/getAllDiscourseNodesSince.ts","hunk":"f-3b7aa896c8cd3682-h3","layer":"layer-convert","line":51,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/getAllDiscourseNodesSince.ts#L51"},{"id":"s3","title":"Embed the Content that search reads","text":"`fetchEmbeddingsForNodes` embeds `directAndDescription` when present, else `direct`, and attaches the vector to that Content. The plain `direct` of a first-child node gets no embedding.","symbol":"fetchEmbeddingsForNodes","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts","hunk":"f-1451ae38f21e3080-h3","layer":"layer-embed","line":41,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts#L41"},{"id":"s4","title":"Write Concept and Contents in one row","text":"`convertDgToSupabaseConcepts` converts each node with `crossAppNodeToDbConcept`, so `contents_inline` carries `direct`, `direct_and_description` and `full`.","symbol":"convertDgToSupabaseConcepts","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","hunk":"f-1b01e86445690d7e-h10","layer":"layer-write","line":700,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L700"},{"id":"s5","title":"Send every batch, then fail once","text":"`upsertConceptBatches` records negative ids per batch and the `source_local_id`s behind them, then throws one `ConceptRowFailuresError` after the last batch.","symbol":"upsertConceptBatches","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","hunk":"f-1b01e86445690d7e-h7","layer":"layer-write","line":323,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L323"},{"id":"s6","title":"Drop a Source the space can't resolve","text":"`omitMissingSources` keeps a RID, a Source in the same upsert, or an existing Concept, and otherwise clears `slots` so the row still lands.","symbol":"omitMissingSources","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","hunk":"f-1b01e86445690d7e-h11","layer":"layer-write","line":772,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L772"},{"id":"s7","title":"Upsert, then publish assets for rows that landed","text":"The sync merges full content into changed nodes, upserts, runs `publishNodeAssets` for rows that didn't fail, reports assets, and only then rethrows the row failures.","symbol":"createOrUpdateDiscourseEmbedding","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","hunk":"f-1b01e86445690d7e-h15","layer":"layer-sync","line":1540,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts#L1540"},{"id":"s8","title":"Update embeddings uses the same write","text":"The settings button calls `upsertNodesWithEmbeddings` and sends failures to `internalError`, which shows a toast.","symbol":"DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules","path":"apps/roam/src/components/settings/DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx","hunk":"f-6bdb9ed82dd43ea3-h2","layer":"layer-reembed","line":62,"side":"head","url":"https://github.com/DiscourseGraphs/discourse-graph/blob/77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3/apps/roam/src/components/settings/DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx#L62"}],"example":{"title":"A first-child Claim, before and after","step_id":"s4","description":"The same Roam row for a node whose type takes its description from the first child, and what sync sends for it.","panels":[{"label":"Roam row (first-child query)","code":"{ source_local_id: \"pg1\", type: \"clm-type\",\n  node_title: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall\",\n  text: \"Subjects recalled more\",\n  author_local_id: \"child-user\", node_author_local_id: \"page-user\" }"},{"label":"Before: two RPCs","code":"upsert_content  [{ source_local_id: \"pg1\", variant: \"direct_and_description\",\n                   text: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall Subjects recalled more\",\n                   author_local_id: \"child-user\", embedding_inline: {...} }]\nupsert_concepts [{ source_local_id: \"pg1\", name: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall\",\n                   author_local_id: \"page-user\",\n                   literal_content: { core_title: \"Sleep aids recall\" } }]"},{"label":"After: one row","code":"upsert_concepts [{ source_local_id: \"pg1\", name: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall\",\n  author_local_id: \"page-user\", schema_represented_by_local_id: \"clm-type\",\n  literal_content: { core_title: \"Sleep aids recall\" },\n  contents_inline: [\n    { variant: \"direct\", text: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall\",\n      author_local_id: \"page-user\" },\n    { variant: \"direct_and_description\",\n      text: \"[[CLM]] - Sleep aids recall Subjects recalled more\",\n      author_local_id: \"child-user\", embedding_inline: {...} } ] }]"}],"outcomes":[{"label":"Content fails","text":"Before: the Concept could land without its Content, or the reverse. After: the row returns -2 and neither lands."},{"label":"New row","text":"The node gains a plain direct Content (the page title) with no embedding, as publish writes it."}],"note":"Illustrative excerpt built from the pinned converters. created, last_modified, scale and content_type are omitted. Not an observed production payload."},"pseudocode":{"title":"Write order in createOrUpdateDiscourseEmbedding","step_id":"s7","before":"upsertNodes:       upsert_content(changed nodes, embedded unless shared-only)\nupsertFullContent: upsert_content(full markdown of shared nodes)\npublishSharedNodeAssets(shared nodes)   # FileReference needs Content\nconvertConcepts:   upsert_concepts(node types + changed nodes), 200 per call\n                   stop at the first batch with a failed row","after":"convertNodes:      rows -> CrossAppNode; embed changed nodes unless shared-only\nbuildFullContent:  shared nodes -> CrossAppNode with full markdown\nnodes = omitMissingSources(withFullContent(converted, fullContent))\nconvertConcepts:   upsert_concepts(node types + nodes), 50 per call\n                   send every batch; collect failed source_local_ids\npublishSharedNodeAssets(nodes whose row landed)\nreport assets; then throw if any row failed","unchanged":"An RPC error still stops the sync before the asset stage. Node types still use discourseNodeSchemaToLocalConcept."},"verification":"Reviewer checks at head 77617e5 on Node 20.20.2: tsc pass, Prettier pass, Roam unit suite 715/715 pass, ESLint 8 warnings none on added lines, Done When grep pass. Database behavior was read from concept.sql and content.sql, not executed. The author's proof kit (PR comment, 2026-10-26) reports 14/14 cases against a local proof database on build 53ee3b2; its sync-path files are byte-identical to this head, but this review did not reproduce the run. The linked GitHub video and Loom were not watched."}}
39	{"pseudocode":{"base_sha":"946090664dae0c1a46eaed33594f0b8d30d208dd","head_sha":"77617e5f605d26a32eedad262b882580a19f82e3","title":"How a Roam node reaches upsert_concepts","intro":"Follow one node from the Roam query to the database. Steps 1 to 3 build the `CrossAppNode`, steps 4 to 6 prepare and write it, steps 7 and 8 cover failures and assets, step 9 is the settings button, and step 10 lists what was removed.","flow":["Roam query row","discourseNodeToCrossApp","fetchEmbeddingsForNodes","withFullContent","omitMissingSources","crossAppNodeToDbConcept","upsertConceptBatches","publishNodeAssets"],"boundary":"Roam sync and Update embeddings only. Publish, Obsidian and node-type conversion are unchanged. No migration; stored first-child nodes gain `direct` when next sent.","steps":[{"title":"1. Read the page creator for first-child nodes","narrative":"The first-child query now also returns `node_author_local_id`: the page's `:create/user`, or the child's creator when the page has none. Page rows don't set it.","code":"for each page matching a first-child node type:\n  child = first child block\n  row.author_local_id      = creator of child\n  row.node_author_local_id = creator of page, else creator of child","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/getAllDiscourseNodesSince.ts","line":51,"side":"head"},{"title":"2. Build a CrossAppNode from each row","narrative":"`direct` is the page title for both page and block-backed rows. A row with `node_title` adds `directAndDescription`, credited to the child's creator. The Concept author prefers the page creator. `coreTitle` and the Source slot come from the page title.","code":"title = row.node_title ?? row.text\nnode.authorId = row.node_author_local_id ?? row.author_local_id\nnode.content.direct = { value: title }\nif row.node_title:\n  node.content.directAndDescription = { value: title + ' ' + row.text,\n                                        authorId: row.author_local_id }\nif sourceIdOfNode(title, schema): node.slots.sourceDocument = it","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","line":74,"side":"head"},{"title":"3. Reuse it for shared full content","narrative":"`fullContentNodeToCrossApp` calls `discourseNodeToCrossApp` and adds `full`. Full-content rows carry no `node_title`, so these nodes have `direct` and `full` only, with `modifiedAt` = max(node edit, page edit).","code":"fullNode = discourseNodeToCrossApp(row, schema)\nfullNode.content.full = buildFullInlineContent(uid, fullNode.content.direct.value)\nconvertRoamNodeToFullContent returns CrossAppNode[] (drops nodes whose markdown fails)","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/roamToCrossAppConverters.ts","line":107,"side":"head","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/convertRoamNodeToFullContent.ts"]},{"title":"4. Embed the Content that search reads","narrative":"`toCrossAppNodesWithEmbeddings` converts every row and embeds only `nodeIdsToEmbed`: changed nodes, or none on a shared-only sync. Core-title backfill nodes are converted but not embedded. `fetchEmbeddingsForNodes` still throws on a count mismatch.","code":"nodes = rows.map(discourseNodeToCrossApp)\nembedded = fetchEmbeddingsForNodes(nodes where id in nodeIdsToEmbed)\n  text   = (directAndDescription ?? direct).value\n  vector -> that same Content\nreturn nodes with embedded ones swapped in","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts","line":41,"side":"head","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts"]},{"title":"5. Merge full content into changed nodes","narrative":"`withFullContent` gives a changed shared node its `full` Content, stamped with the page edit time, and keeps the node's own `modifiedAt`. Shared nodes sent only for full content are appended, so their Concept is now upserted too.","code":"for node in changed:\n  if fullContent[node.id].full exists:\n    node.content.full = fullContent.full with modifiedAt = fullContent.modifiedAt\nappend fullContent nodes that are not in changed","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":744,"side":"head"},{"title":"6. Drop Sources the database can't resolve","narrative":"Same rule as publish's `omitMissingSource`, without the toast. `conceptIds` is the set of instance Concepts already in the space, read once per sync (or per button press).","code":"for node in nodes:\n  src = node.slots?.sourceDocument\n  keep if src is undefined or isRid(src)\n          or src in this upsert or src in conceptIds\n  else node.slots = undefined   # Concept lands without the reference","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":772,"side":"head"},{"title":"7. Write each node as one Concept row","narrative":"Node-type schema Concepts (with their Content, from #1578) and node Concepts go through `orderConceptsByDependency`, then `upsertConceptBatches`. `upsert_concepts` returns one id per row; inside it, a failing inline Content rolls back that row's Concept.","code":"concepts = nodeTypeConcepts + nodes.map(crossAppNodeToDbConcept)\nfor batch in chunk(order(concepts), 50):\n  ids = rpc('upsert_concepts', batch)\n  if rpc error: throw now\n  record batch[i].source_local_id where ids[i] < 0\nif any recorded: throw ConceptRowFailuresError(ids)","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":700,"side":"head"},{"title":"8. Publish assets for rows that landed","narrative":"`upsertNodesWithAssets` catches only `ConceptRowFailuresError`; other errors still stop before assets. `publishNodeAssets` skips nodes without `full`, so unshared nodes are a no-op. The sync reports assets and then rethrows the row failures, as main did after its Concept step.","code":"try: convertDgToSupabaseConcepts(nodes)\ncatch ConceptRowFailuresError as failures: keep going\nassetResults = publishNodeAssets(nodes without a failed row)\nreportSharedNodeAssets(assetResults)\nif failures: throw failures","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts","line":1540,"side":"head"},{"title":"9. Update embeddings uses the same write","narrative":"The button loads every node of the type, drops imported ones, and calls `upsertNodesWithEmbeddings`. That embeds all of them, drops unresolved Sources, and upserts the node type's schema Concept plus each node's Concept with Contents. Errors reach `internalError` with a toast.","code":"nodes = getAllDiscourseNodesSince(undefined, [nodeType]) minus imported\ntry:\n  synced = getNodeInstanceSourceLocalIds().synced\n  convertDgToSupabaseConcepts(omitMissingSources(embedAll(nodes), synced),\n                              allNodeTypes = [nodeType])\ncatch error: internalError(error, 'Failed to update embeddings')","path":"apps/roam/src/components/settings/DiscourseNodeSuggestiveRules.tsx","line":62,"side":"head","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/syncDgNodesToSupabase.ts"]},{"title":"10. Removed writers and converters","narrative":"Removed: both `upsert_content` writers in the sync file, the unused duplicate writer here (no importer at base), and `discourseNodeBlockToLocalConcept` with its tests. `convertRoamNodeToLocalContent` stays only for node-type Content and always writes `direct`.","code":"delete uploadContentBatches, upsertNodesToSupabaseAsContent(WithEmbeddings)\ndelete upsertSharedNodesFullContentWithAssets\ndelete discourseNodeBlockToLocalConcept (+ getNodeExtraData call per node)\nkeep convertRoamNodeToLocalContent for getNodeSchemaContents","path":"apps/roam/src/utils/upsertNodesAsContentWithEmbeddings.ts","line":123,"side":"base","files":["apps/roam/src/utils/conceptConversion.ts","apps/roam/src/utils/__tests__/conceptConversion.test.ts"]}]}}
